@startuml gsm-sourcer-pipeline-records

' ============================================================
' VISUAL THEME
' ============================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDFD
  BorderColor #444444
  ArrowColor #444444
  FontName "Helvetica"
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
  BorderColor #999999
}

frame "CD - GSM Sourcer - Pipeline Records (engine-internal records produced by the post-Target-quiescence Pipeline: ValidatedAscriptionDraft, RegisteredAscription)" {

  note as N_Scope
    **Scope** -- These are engine-internal Java records produced by
    the **Pipeline** stages that run AFTER `targetResolution` is
    published. They are NOT Blackboard panels, NOT KS-visible, and
    NOT serialised across a trust boundary; they are persisted
    alongside the Run audit artefact for replay only.

    The Pipeline has three stages (see
    `gsm-sourcer-blackboard-framework-contracts.puml`):
    - **Validation** -- folds each converged Target-spine tuple
      `(Definition + resolved Archetype + Statement)` into a
      `ValidatedAscriptionDraft`.
    - **Registration** -- persists each draft into the Definition
      Manager and records the result as a `RegisteredAscription`
      (or `SKIPPED` when `Definition.Verdict = drop`).
    - **Persistence** -- writes the Run audit bundle (drafts,
      registrations, both `BlackboardResolution`s, diagnostics)
      to `BundleStore`.
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' VALIDATED ASCRIPTION DRAFT
  ' ============================================================

  class ValidatedAscriptionDraft <<engine,record,immutable>> {
    +id: String
    +definitionContributionId: String
    +subjectKind: GsmSubjectKind
    +identityKey: String
    +archetypeRefs: List<URI>
    +statement: JsonObject
    +granularityVerdict: DefinitionVerdict?
    +confidence: double?
    +validationStatus: ValidationStatus
    +validationDiagnostics: List<Diagnostic>
    +resolverDecisions: List<ResolverDecision>
    +evidenceContributionIds: List<String>
    +createdAt: Instant
  }

  enum ValidationStatus {
    OK
    FAILED
  }

  enum GsmSubjectKind {
    Structure
    Mechanism
    Effector
    Receptor
    Interaction
    Archetype
    Directive
    Norm
  }

  class ResolverDecision <<engine,value>> {
    +panel: String
    +selectedContributionId: String
    +competingContributionIds: List<String>
    +resolver: ContributionResolver
    +rationale: String?
  }

  note bottom of ValidatedAscriptionDraft
    **ValidatedAscriptionDraft** -- engine-internal Pipeline record
    produced by the **Validation** stage from one converged Target-
    spine tuple (one Definition + its resolved Archetype(s) +
    Statement).

    **Wave 9 lineage** (panel collapse):
    - `granularityVerdict` is sourced from the resolved
      `Definition.Verdict` slot (replaces the dropped Granularity
      panel).
    - `confidence` is the resolved Statement Contribution's
      `confidence` value, after `ConfidenceSynthesisKS` folding
      via the `compose` resolver (replaces the dropped Confidence
      panel).
    - `evidenceContributionIds` reference the Statement
      Contributions whose `evidence: List<EvidenceRef>` arrays
      carried the per-tuple signals (replaces the dropped Evidence
      panel).

    `resolverDecisions[]` records, per panel, which competing
    Contributions were folded into the selected one and which
    `ContributionResolver` strategy was applied -- the audit
    trail required by I-12 (deterministic replay).

    **Validation Rules**:

    - `archetypeRefs` MUST contain at least one entry.
    - `subjectKind` MUST equal the resolved Definition Contribution's
      `subjectKind` (consistency check).
    - `resolverDecisions[]` panel values MUST be in
      {`Definition`, `Archetype`, `Statement`}.
    - `confidence`, when present, MUST be in `[0, 1]`.
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' REGISTERED ASCRIPTION
  ' ============================================================

  class RegisteredAscription <<engine,record,immutable>> {
    +id: String
    +validatedDraftId: String
    +ascriptionUri: URI
    +registrationStatus: RegistrationStatus
    +registrationDiagnostics: List<Diagnostic>
    +registeredAt: Instant
  }

  enum RegistrationStatus {
    REGISTERED
    FAILED
    SKIPPED
  }

  note bottom of RegisteredAscription
    **RegisteredAscription** -- engine-internal Pipeline record
    produced by the **Registration** stage. Pairs a
    `ValidatedAscriptionDraft` with the Definition Manager-issued
    `AscriptionUri`.

    **Status semantics**:

    - `REGISTERED` -- the draft was accepted by the Definition
      Manager; `ascriptionUri` is the canonical handle.
    - `FAILED` -- registration was attempted and refused (e.g.
      Definition Manager rejected the Statement against the
      Archetype schema). Diagnostics record the cause; the draft
      remains in the audit bundle for operator review.
    - `SKIPPED` -- the resolved `Definition.Verdict` was `drop`
      (or `mergeWith` / `splitInto` consolidating into another
      identity); no DefMan call was made.
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' RELATIONSHIPS
  ' ============================================================

  ValidatedAscriptionDraft *-- "0..*" ResolverDecision : resolverDecisions
  ValidatedAscriptionDraft --> ValidationStatus
  ValidatedAscriptionDraft --> GsmSubjectKind
  RegisteredAscription --> RegistrationStatus
  RegisteredAscription ..> ValidatedAscriptionDraft : <<refers to\nvalidatedDraftId>>
}

@enduml
